        "original_id": "1d2b2a33-045c-573e-b230-34ebc8d75612",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Dustin Archbold, John D. Rockefeller\n- Organizations: Standard Oil Company, Syracuse University\n- Places: Archbold Gymnasium, Archbold Stadium, Carrier Dome, Manley Field House\n\nFacts:\n- John Dustin Archbold donated the money to build Archbold Gymnasium at Syracuse University in 1908.\n- John Dustin Archbold was a major benefactor of Syracuse University.\n- John Dustin Archbold also funded the construction of Archbold Stadium, which was just west of Archbold Gymnasium.\n- The Carrier Dome now occupies the former site of Archbold Stadium.\n- John Dustin Archbold's small oil company was bought by John D. Rockefeller's Standard Oil Company.\n- Archbold Gymnasium served for almost 60 years before Manley Field House was built to replace it.",
